anya: quick sanity check before i open the TF PR — converting inference-api from Deployment -> StatefulSet. plan is: replicas=3, podManagementPolicy: OrderedReady, rollingUpdate.partition=1 for staged rollout, maxUnavailable=0, maxSurge=1. also bump startupProbe.initialDelaySeconds from 30 -> 90 because model init. secrets: switch to customer kms-backed secret name `inference-api-kms-secret` and mount at /etc/creds (one secret per ordinal). any obvious footguns?

Miguel: i've done this for batch-worker last month. a few notes: partition=1 is safe for gradual rollout, but with statefulsets you usually prefer partition + ordered ready so only one pod is cycled at a time. set maxUnavailable=0 makes sense. maxSurge=1 is allowed but remember it will create an extra pod (and PVC) temporarily — watch storage quota.

Miguel: also: volumeClaimTemplates is the right pattern so you don't have to rename PVCs. if your app relies on stable networkid or hostname, ensure headless svc exists.

Kevin: tf specifics — update `kubernetes_stateful_set` resource. don't change `.spec.selector` labels in-place (that forces recreation). if you need to change selectors do a blue/green or recreate with traffic switch. sample snippet we used: ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "inference" {
  metadata { name = "inference-api" }
  spec {
    replicas = 3
    pod_management_policy = "OrderedReady"
    update_strategy {
      type = "RollingUpdate"
      rolling_update { partition = 1 }
    }
    template { /* containers, probes, mounts */ }
    volume_claim_template { /* pvc spec */ }
  }
}
```

Kevin: one more tf gotcha — changing `volumeClaimTemplates` can be disruptive if storage class parameters differ. double-check storageclass reclaimPolicy and accessModes.

Sam: cc @anya — CI/deploy note: our deploy-bot will consider a canary healthy after 10m by default. for model cold-starts bump the canary window to 15m and raise the error threshold to 6% so we don't auto-rollback on transient init latency. we should also add a warmup job to prefetch weights on the new pod. :thumbsup:

